DecimalPlaces [SimTalk] - Variable
Sets the number of Decimal Places which the Variable designated by the reference operator <&> shows in
the Frame.
Remarks
The Variable can show up to 15 decimal places. The default setting -1 shows all existing places. If you
enter a positive value, the Variable shows the number of decimal places, which you entered, in the Frame.
Note
This setting only applies to the Data Types > real, length, money, weight, time, speed, and
acceleration.
The number of decimal places for the data type time affects values differently than for the data type real.
The value -1 for the data type time means that the default time display format is displayed with four
decimal places. A positive value means that Plant Simulation shows the number of decimal places that you
entered at most.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<&>Variable.DecimalPlaces:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
&MyVariable.DecimalPlaces := 12
See also
Data Type [Variable]
Decimal Places [text box] - Variable
& [SimTalk] - Variable
DecimalPlaces [SimTalk] - Variable
