InitValue [SimTalk] - Variable
Resets a value, which the Variable designated by the reference operator <&> recorded during a simulation
run, to an Initial Value.
Remarks
Plant Simulation sets the value during the reset phase and resets it in the init phase of the next simulation
run.
Note
The Data types table, list, stack, queue, and randtime do not provide this feature.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<&>Variable.InitValue:any
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type any.
Example
&MyVariable.DataType := "integer"
&MyVariable.InitValue := 0
SimTalk
HasInitValue [SimTalk] - Variable
See also
Data Type [Variable]
Initial Value [Variable]
& [SimTalk] - Variable
InitValue [SimTalk] - Variable
