IntegerPlaces [SimTalk] - Variable
Sets the number of Integer Places which the Variable designated by the reference operator <&> shows in
the Frame.
Remarks
The Variable can show up to 15 integer places. The default setting -1 means that Plant Simulation applies
no minimum to the number of integer places. Enter a positive value to fill up the space before the decimal
point with blank spaces until the specified number of places has been reached when the Variable is shown.
Note
This setting only applies to the Data types > real, length, weight, time, speed, and acceleration.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<&>Variable.IntegerPlaces:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Example
&MyVariable.IntegerPlaces := 6
-- The value "123"     will show as "   123"
-- The value "123456"  will show as "123456"
-- The value "1234567" will show as "1234567"
See also
Data Type [user-defined attribute]
Integer Places [text box] - Variable, text box
IntegerPlaces [SimTalk] - Variable
